{"id": "2026-11-13-news-iran-claims-strike-on-us-radar-in-bahrain", "date": "2026-11-13", "stream": "news", "headline": "Iran claims strike on US radar in Bahrain", "summary": "The IRGC said on 13 November it destroyed a US early-warning radar in Bahrain in retaliation for an attack on a Sirik telecoms tower; unconfirmed.", "url": "https://www.euronews.com/2026/11/13/irgc-says-it-destroyed-us-radar-in-bahrain-after-attack-on-southern-iran", "source_domain": "euronews.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["disputed"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "Iran's Revolutionary Guards (IRGC) said on Friday 13 November that they had destroyed a US early-warning radar in Bahrain, calling it retaliation for an air attack on a telecommunications tower in Sirik County in southern Iran on Thursday 12 November. Iranian state media carried the claim, and neither the US military nor Bahrain has confirmed it. It is also unclear who attacked the Sirik tower or how badly it was damaged. The IRGC called the strike a \"serious warning\" to Washington to stop \"aerial provocations and oil smuggling\" in the Strait of Hormuz. Bahrain hosts the headquarters of the US Navy's Fifth Fleet. SRF's live ticker described it as Iran's first attack on a US military facility since September. Hours earlier, President Donald Trump wrote that \"we don't need a deal with Iran\" and told Vice President JD Vance, who led the earlier talks and has blamed the war for the Republicans' midterm losses, to focus instead on what Trump calls corruption in Democratic-run cities. Several commercial ships have hit mines or been struck in the strait over the past week.", "why": "if the claim is true, this is the first direct Iranian hit on US forces in about two months, and Washington has now said openly that it is not seeking a deal. That shifts the standoff over Hormuz, which drives energy prices, back towards military escalation.", "thread_id": "2026-11-13-news-iran-claims-strike-on-us-radar-in-bahrain", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-13", "event_date": "2026-11-13", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Iran", "IRGC", "Bahrain", "United States", "Strait of Hormuz"]}
{"id": "2026-11-13-news-kremlin-says-no-decision-on-european-seat", "date": "2026-11-13", "stream": "news", "headline": "Kremlin says no decision on European seat", "summary": "Kushner said Putin agreed to include Europe in Ukraine talks after their 12 November meeting; the Kremlin said on 13 November no decision was made.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/13/russia-and-ukraine-report-overnight-attacks-amid-us-diplomatic-push", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "US envoy Jared Kushner said late on Thursday 12 November, after he and Steve Witkoff met Vladimir Putin in Moscow, that Putin had agreed to include Europe in the Ukraine peace talks. On Friday 13 November the Kremlin said it had not yet agreed. \"We cannot conclude this deal without the Europeans being at the table,\" Kushner said in Dublin, where the envoys briefed Volodymyr Zelensky. Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov said Moscow would decide on \"an expanded format\" only \"once we understand their real intentions\". EU leaders were meeting informally in Dublin on Friday, the day after the European Political Community summit, to settle who would speak for the bloc. The talks between Russia and Ukraine are expected to resume next week, the week starting Monday 16 November. Overnight, Russia said it intercepted 1,198 Ukrainian drones over more than 15 regions; four people were killed in Volgograd. Russian strikes hit Odesa, killing at least two people, and set a Kyiv hospital on fire.", "why": "Europe's place at the table is now the main open question in the talks, and Moscow appears to be using it as a bargaining chip while it holds firm on its territorial demands.", "thread_id": "2026-11-13-news-kremlin-says-no-decision-on-european-seat", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-13", "event_date": "2026-11-12", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Russia", "Ukraine", "Jared Kushner", "Vladimir Putin", "European Union"]}
{"id": "2026-11-13-news-germany-plans-210bn-new-debt-for-2027", "date": "2026-11-13", "stream": "news", "headline": "Germany plans €210bn new debt for 2027", "summary": "The Bundestag budget committee approved a 2027 budget with just over €210 billion of new borrowing, the second-highest in post-war Germany.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-parliament-agrees-on-debt-laden-2027-budget/live-79936897", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["economy", "politics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "On the night of Thursday 12 to Friday 13 November, the German Bundestag's budget committee signed off on the 2027 federal budget. It includes just over €210 billion of new borrowing, the second-highest amount in the Federal Republic's history. The figure counts borrowing through the off-budget \"special funds\" for the military and infrastructure as well as the core budget. New debt makes up about a third of total spending, against just under €400 billion in tax revenue. Only 2021, at the height of the pandemic, was higher, at €215.4 billion. Chancellor Friedrich Merz's proposed cut to the electricity tax did not survive: Finance Minister Lars Klingbeil (SPD) said there was no fiscal room for it, and the SPD said it would have to be paid for with more debt. The committee's sign-off is the last major step before the full Bundestag votes on the budget.", "why": "Germany is Switzerland's largest trading partner. A Berlin borrowing for defence and infrastructure on this scale means more demand for Swiss suppliers, but no relief on energy prices for German industry.", "thread_id": "2026-11-13-news-germany-plans-210bn-new-debt-for-2027", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-13", "event_date": "2026-11-13", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Germany", "Bundestag", "Friedrich Merz", "Lars Klingbeil"]}
{"id": "2026-11-13-news-un-counts-1-167-killed-in-haiti-in-q3", "date": "2026-11-13", "stream": "news", "headline": "UN counts 1,167 killed in Haiti in Q3", "summary": "BINUH reported at least 1,167 killed and 459 injured in Haiti in July-September 2026, over half during security-force operations.", "url": "https://news.un.org/feed/view/en/story/2026/11/1168789", "source_domain": "news.un.org", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["world"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "At least 1,167 people were killed and 459 injured in Haiti between July and September, the UN's integrated office in the country (BINUH) said in a human-rights report published on Thursday 12 November. Gangs were responsible for more than 45% of the incidents and self-defence groups for about 5%. More than half of the documented killings and injuries happened during ground or aerial operations by security forces against gangs, sometimes with drone support from a private military company. Gangs that had been driven out of Bel Air and La Saline earlier this year have returned. The UN Security Council has authorised a Gang Suppression Force, but it is not yet fully deployed.", "why": "the operations against the gangs are now themselves the largest source of casualties, which raises questions about how the authorised international force will be run.", "thread_id": "2026-11-13-news-un-counts-1-167-killed-in-haiti-in-q3", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-13", "event_date": "2026-11-12", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Haiti", "BINUH", "United Nations"]}
{"id": "2026-11-13-news-microsoft-365-outage-hits-outlook-and-teams", "date": "2026-11-13", "stream": "news", "headline": "Microsoft 365 outage hits Outlook and Teams", "summary": "A global Microsoft 365 outage from 12 November disrupted Outlook, Teams and Copilot; Microsoft said it saw no malicious activity.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/microsoft-rules-out-malicious-activity-as-cause-for-global-outage/a-79935611", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["tech"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "A global outage of Microsoft 365 that began on Thursday 12 November disrupted Outlook, Teams and Copilot in dozens of countries. Microsoft said its fixes \"are not taking as expected\" and that it was \"not aware\" of any malicious activity. Downdetector logged reports from 74 countries and territories within about an hour, and nearly 130,000 US reports of Outlook problems. Microsoft said some restarted servers stopped responding again once traffic returned. At 02:54 GMT on Friday it said it was trying other ways to restore service. It is the second disruption to Microsoft 365 this year.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-13-news-microsoft-365-outage-hits-outlook-and-teams", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-13", "event_date": "2026-11-12", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Microsoft", "Outlook", "Teams"]}
{"id": "2026-11-13-news-zurich-to-host-epc-summit-in-april-2027", "date": "2026-11-13", "stream": "news", "headline": "Zurich to host EPC summit in April 2027", "summary": "Switzerland will host the tenth European Political Community summit in Zurich on 15 April 2027, the Federal Council said after Parmelin attended Dublin.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/hLtItNJ5hKOy", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR"], "topics": ["switzerland", "geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Switzerland will host the next European Political Community (EPC) summit, in Zurich on 15 April 2027, the Federal Council announced after Federal President Guy Parmelin attended the ninth summit in Dublin on Thursday 12 November. In Dublin, Parmelin held bilateral talks with Lithuanian President Gitanas Nausėda, whose country takes over the EU Council presidency next, Hungarian Prime Minister Péter Magyar, European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen and UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham. He presented Switzerland as a place for \"confronting different points of view\". The EPC brings the whole continent together, inside and outside the EU, and has met twice a year since Prague in October 2022, alternating between EU and non-EU hosts.", "why": "if the Ukraine talks have moved on by April, a Zurich summit would put Swiss diplomacy, and Swiss security planning, at the centre of Europe's postwar discussions.", "thread_id": "2026-11-13-news-zurich-to-host-epc-summit-in-april-2027", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-13", "event_date": "2027-04-15", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Switzerland", "European Political Community", "Guy Parmelin", "Zurich"]}
{"id": "2026-11-13-news-eu-rule-change-on-cross-border-jobless-pay", "date": "2026-11-13", "stream": "news", "headline": "EU rule change on cross-border jobless pay", "summary": "At the Swiss-EU free-movement Joint Committee, the EU notified Switzerland of revised social-security rules changing unemployment insurance for cross-border workers; the Federal Council will consider adoption.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/vpJVENEuDlBz", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR", "single-source"], "topics": ["switzerland", "economy"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The EU has told Switzerland that its revised social-security coordination rules (Regulations 883/2004 and 987/2009) are now in force, and the Federal Council will consider \"in due course\" whether to adopt them. Switzerland says they bring \"significant changes\" to unemployment insurance for cross-border workers. The point came up at the 29th Swiss–EU Joint Committee on the free-movement agreement in Bern. The Swiss communiqué was published on Wednesday 12 November but dates the meeting to 12 October. The delegations were led by Regula Mader of the State Secretariat for Migration and the Commission's Nicolas von Lingen. The communiqué does not spell out the changes. As the EU adopted it, the revision means that the country where a cross-border worker was last employed, rather than the country where they live, generally becomes responsible for paying their unemployment benefits.", "why": "if Switzerland adopts the rules, the Swiss unemployment fund, not France, Italy or Germany, would pay many cross-border workers when they lose their jobs, a cost that has long been contested in the Bilaterals debate.", "thread_id": "2026-11-13-news-eu-rule-change-on-cross-border-jobless-pay", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-13", "event_date": null, "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Switzerland", "European Union", "Free Movement of Persons Agreement", "SEM"]}
{"id": "2026-11-13-news-swiss-producer-prices-up-0-9-in-october", "date": "2026-11-13", "stream": "news", "headline": "Swiss producer prices up 0.9% in October", "summary": "The Swiss producer and import price index rose 0.9% month on month in October 2026 to 101.6 points, driven by petroleum products.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/JrBG3ZuNaVyE", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR"], "topics": ["switzerland", "economy"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Switzerland's producer and import price index rose 0.9% in October from September, to 101.6 points (December 2025 = 100), the Federal Statistical Office said on Friday 13 November. Prices were also 0.9% higher than in October 2025. The monthly rise came mainly from petroleum products, hydrocarbons, electrical equipment, IT and electronic goods, and machinery.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-13-news-swiss-producer-prices-up-0-9-in-october", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-13", "event_date": "2026-11-13", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Federal Statistical Office", "Switzerland"]}
{"id": "2026-11-13-news-family-leave-initiative-qualifies-for-vote", "date": "2026-11-13", "stream": "news", "headline": "Family leave initiative qualifies for vote", "summary": "The Federal Chancellery found 111,151 valid signatures for the family leave popular initiative, which has formally qualified.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/VD-6QWsCwspL", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR"], "topics": ["switzerland", "politics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "The popular initiative for a family leave (\"Une société et une économie fortes grâce au congé parental\") has formally qualified, the Federal Chancellery said on Thursday 12 November, after it found 111,151 of the 112,529 signatures submitted on 30 September to be valid. The Federal Council and Parliament must now take a position on it before it goes to a national vote.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-13-news-family-leave-initiative-qualifies-for-vote", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-13", "event_date": "2026-11-12", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Federal Chancellery", "Switzerland"]}
